  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nHigh pressure is set up over the eastern half of the United States. \nWith the ridging not going anywhere any time soon, clear skies and \ndry weather will continue across the state for the next week. Winds \nhave picked up to 10-15 mph today but will become very light to near \ncalm again overnight. The main focus of this forecast continues to \nbe the temperatures and maybe additional frost potential tonight. \n\nTemperatures will drop down into the upper 30s to low 40s tonight.\nGreat radiational cooling will be in place again tonight with \nclear skies and light winds. That mixed with the cold temperatures,\nfrost formation may be possible again in south-central and \neastern IL. If radiational cooling overperforms, temperatures \ncould get near freezing in some spots. Continue to take \nprecautions to protect sensitive vegetation with these colder \ntemperatures and threat of frost.\n\nTemperatures have began a warming trend today. Highs tomorrow will \nbe in the low 70s, but by Thursday temperatures will be back well \nabove normal with highs in the upper 70s, nearing 80. Normals for \nthis time of year is around 65-69 degrees across central and \nsoutheastern IL.",
